  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "correctness",
    "affected_api": "cvxpy.reductions.complex2real.canonicalizers.matrix_canon.lambda_sum_largest_canon",
    "observed_behavior": "lambda_sum_largest_canon doubles k unconditionally, so a real symmetric argument to lambda_sum_largest is rebuilt with 2k on the original n\u00d7n matrix when the problem also contains an unrelated complex expression. In the PR reproducer this gives an optimal value of 30.0 with lambda_sum_largest(X, 2) == 20, violating the constraint <= 5; the test run shows 30.00000005323264 instead of 7.499999998339203. When 2k > n it can instead report spurious unboundedness.",
    "expected_behavior": "The optimal value should be 7.5, matching the same problem without the unrelated complex variable z. k should be doubled only when the argument has an imaginary part (imag_args[0] is not None).",
    "manifestation": "wrong_value",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "lambda_sum_largest applied to a real symmetric matrix argument (e.g. X = cp.Variable((3,3), symmetric=True))",
      "the problem also contains an unrelated complex expression or variable (e.g. z = cp.Variable(complex=True) with cp.abs(z) <= 1), so Complex2Real reduction runs over the whole problem",
      "k > 0 such that 2k is applied to the real argument (e.g. lambda_sum_largest(X, 2))",
      "spurious unboundedness occurs when 2k > n"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "X = cp.Variable((3,3), symmetric=True); z = cp.Variable(complex=True); p = cp.Problem(cp.Maximize(cp.trace(X)), [cp.lambda_sum_largest(X, 2) <= 5, X >> 0, X << 10*np.eye(3), cp.abs(z) <= 1]); p.solve(solver=cp.CLARABEL)",
        "buggy_output": "30.0 with lambda_sum_largest(X, 2) == 20 (constraint violated)",
        "expected_output": "7.5",
        "value_kind": "float",
        "source": "PR#3376 repro"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": []
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": null,
    "precision": "places=4 (assertAlmostEqual) in test; CLARABEL solver used; reference value 7.5",
    "magnitude": null,
    "tolerance": "places=4 for assertAlmostEqual on objective (7.5 reference); lambda_sum_largest(X,2).value <= 5 + 1e-4",
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Mathematical property violated: lambda_sum_largest(X,k) doubled k unconditionally for real symmetric arguments in Complex2Real, so the atom was rebuilt as sum of 2k largest eigenvalues on an n x n matrix, violating the constraint lambda_sum_largest(X,2) <= 5",
      "Concrete values: buggy objective 30.0 with lambda_sum_largest(X, 2) == 20 (constraint violated); correct objective 7.5 matching the problem without the unrelated complex variable z",
      "Failing test output: AssertionError 30.00000005323264 != 7.499999998339203 within 4 places; fixed branch passes",
      "Spurious unboundedness occurs when 2k > n",
      "Fix: real.k *= 2 moved inside the imag_args[0] is not None branch, so real arguments are not doubled",
      "Problem setup: X = Variable((3,3), symmetric=True), constraints lambda_sum_largest(X,2) <= 5, X >> 0, X << 10*np.eye(3), objective Maximize(trace(X)), plus cp.abs(z) <= 1 with z complex",
      "Benchmark passages show only timing ratios (e.g., 0.99, 1.00) with no correctness numerics"
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "Bug requires an unrelated complex expression in the same problem to trigger the doubling for a real argument",
      "Test asserts results against a 4-place tolerance, so solver precision (CLARABEL) can affect matching",
      "Benchmark timing data is irrelevant to correctness reproduction"
    ]
  },
